{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016hwYqoH9auqpSDvCX7NZpf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 unconstrained baseline\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"使用 Phase 2 pipeline 重跑 DocRED unconstrained，与 constrained 实验共用相同 prompt/generation config/post-processing，确保消融表 F1/violation 对比公平。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"documents_checked\": 975,\n7\t      \"parse_failures\": 23,\n8\t      \"total_entities\": 19800,\n9\t      \"total_triples\": 16200,\n10\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.068,\n11\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.265,\n12\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.158,\n13\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n14\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0808,\n15\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.585,\n16\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.977,\n17\t      \"dr_reduction_vs_full_s1_pct\": 35.5\n18\t    },\n19\t    \"tables\": [\n20\t      {\n21\t        \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 Full Ablation Table\",\n22\t        \"columns\": [\n23\t          \"Mode\",\n24\t          \"DR(%)\",\n25\t          \"RV(%)\",\n26\t          \"ET(%)\",\n27\t          \"CF(%)\",\n28\t          \"R-F1\",\n29\t          \"Triples\"\n30\t        ],\n31\t        \"rows\": [\n32\t          [\n33\t            \"Unconstrained\",\n34\t            15.8,\n35\t            26.5,\n36\t            6.8,\n37\t            0.1,\n38\t            8.08,\n39\t            16200\n40\t          ],\n41\t          [\n42\t            \"Grammar-only\",\n43\t            26.17,\n44\t            0.03,\n45\t            0.0,\n46\t            0.08,\n47\t            8.24,\n48\t            17341\n49\t          ],\n50\t          [\n51\t            \"Semantic-only\",\n52\t            11.2,\n53\t            24.8,\n54\t            5.9,\n55\t            3.8,\n56\t            7.95,\n57\t            16050\n58\t          ],\n59\t          [\n60\t            \"Full S1\",\n61\t            10.19,\n62\t            0.03,\n63\t            0.0,\n64\t            2.99,\n65\t            8.17,\n66\t            17372\n67\t          ]\n68\t        ]\n69\t      }\n70\t    ],\n71\t    \"figures\": [],\n72\t    \"analysis\": \"DR reduction 35.5% 远低于 SciERC 94%，直接挑战 cross-dataset generalization claim。 Grammar-only DR=26.17% > unconstrained DR=15.8% 的现象需要 §5.4 专门解释： grammar 消除 ~27% 的 RV violations 后，原先有 invalid relation name 的 triples 现在有了 valid relation name，可以被 DR checker 评估，暴露大量新 DR violations。 这不是 grammar 变差了，而是 Phase 0 的 DR=18.7% 本身就低估了（被 RV 掩盖了真实 DR）。 如果用 grammar-only 26.17% 作为 \\\"真实 baseline\\\"， full_s1 的 DR reduction = (26.17-10.19)/26.17 = 61.1%——但这个 framing 有 cherry-picking 嫌疑。 论文需要同时报告两个 baseline 的 reduction%，让 reader 自行判断。\\n\\n\\nPhase 2 code path 使用统一 prompt template（含 JSON schema instruction）和 generation config （temperature=0.6, top_p=0.95, thinking mode /no_think），与 Phase 0 minimal prompt 存在细微差异。 预期 DR 从 Phase 0 的 18.7% 降至 ~15.8%，原因三重： (a) Phase 2 统一 JSON instruction 隐式提供了更清晰的 type 格式指导，\\n    模型对 domain/range 的 implicit adherence 轻微提升；\\n(b) Phase 0 使用 raw minimal prompt，Phase 2 code path 的 prompt wrapper 结构更整洁，\\n    部分 Phase 0 边界 case 在 Phase 2 中被分类为 parse failure（23 failures vs Phase 0 的 36 failures），\\n    denominator 缩小使 DR 的百分比下降；\\n(c) generation config 的差异（max_new_tokens=4096 统一设定 vs Phase 0 可能不同）\\n    影响长文档的 truncation behavior，改变 tail triples 的 violation 分布。\\nDR=15.8% 使 full_s1 的 DR reduction 仅为 (15.8-10.19)/15.8 = 35.5%， 远低于 SciERC 的 94%（0.93/15.37）和 Phase 0 基线计算的 45.5%（10.19/18.7）。 这是 worst tier 的核心数字痛点：fair-comparison baseline 偏低导致 improvement narrative 被压缩。 RV/ET 保持 Phase 0 水平（~27%/~7%），因为无 grammar 约束。\\n\"\n73\t  },\n74\t  {\n75\t    \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 semantic-only constrained decoding\",\n76\t    \"description\": \"仅启用 semantic layer（TypeConstraintProcessor），不启用 grammar layer（XGrammar），验证 grammar enabling dependency 是否在复杂 ontology 上复现。\",\n77\t    \"results\": {\n78\t      \"documents_checked\": 970,\n79\t      \"total_triples\": 16050,\n80\t      \"total_entities\": 19600,\n81\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.059,\n82\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.248,\n83\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.112,\n84\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.038,\n85\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0795,\n86\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.58,\n87\t      \"semantic_enabling_ratio\": 1.1,\n88\t      \"semantic_dr_reduction_vs_unconstrained_pct\": 29.1\n89\t    },\n90\t    \"tables\": [\n91\t      {\n92\t        \"name\": \"Enabling Dependency Cross-Dataset Comparison\",\n93\t        \"columns\": [\n94\t          \"Dataset\",\n95\t          \"Ontology_Size\",\n96\t          \"semantic_only_DR(%)\",\n97\t          \"full_s1_DR(%)\",\n98\t          \"Enabling_Ratio\",\n99\t          \"Interpretation\"\n100\t        ],\n101\t        \"rows\": [\n102\t          [\n103\t            \"SciERC\",\n104\t            \"7 rels\",\n105\t            11.65,\n106\t            0.93,\n107\t            12.5,\n108\t            \"Strong enabling: grammar prerequisite\"\n109\t          ],\n110\t          [\n111\t            \"DocRED\",\n112\t            \"96 rels\",\n113\t            11.2,\n114\t            10.19,\n115\t            1.1,\n116\t            \"No enabling: layers independent\"\n117\t          ]\n118\t        ]\n119\t      }\n120\t    ],\n121\t    \"figures\": [],\n122\t    \"analysis\": \"Enabling ratio=1.1 摧毁 Claim 3 的 composable with enabling dependency 叙事。 Reframe 策略：grammar 和 semantic 是两个独立 constraint layer， 各自解决不同 violation type（grammar→ET/RV 100% elimination, semantic→partial DR reduction）， 在 tight ontology 上 grammar 是 semantic 的 prerequisite（SciERC，12.5x）， 在 loose ontology 上两者 independently contribute（DocRED，1.1x）。 论文放弃 \\\"enabling dependency\\\" 作为 universal mechanism， 改为 \\\"enabling relationship modulated by constraint tightness and ontology vocabulary design\\\"。 这个 reframe 将 enabling ratio 的跨数据集差异转化为 empirical finding 而非 method failure。\\n\\n\\nWorst tier 核心预测：semantic_only DR ≈ 11.2%，full_s1 DR = 10.19%， enabling ratio = 11.2/10.19 = 1.10。对比 SciERC enabling ratio = 11.65/0.93 = 12.5。 Grammar 对 semantic 的 enabling 在 DocRED 上几乎不存在，原因三层： (a) DocRED 使用 Wikidata property ID（P31, P17, P131 等短 ID），\\n    模型生成 invalid relation name 后，这些 ID 仍有较高概率恰好是某个 valid relation\\n    （96 relations 覆盖了大量常见 Pxxx pattern），\\n    因此 semantic layer 在无 grammar 时仍能对多数 triples 做 constraint lookup；\\n(b) SciERC 使用自然语言 relation name（\\\"Used-for\\\", \\\"Feature-of\\\"），\\n    无 grammar 时 RV violation 率高（1.51%），这些 triples 的 relation 不在 ontology 中，\\n    semantic layer 直接 skip，无法 enforce DR constraint——这才是 enabling 的来源；\\n(c) DocRED semantic layer 的 per-relation constraints 本身宽松（avg 5.68 valid pairs，\\n    但高频 relations 如 P131_located_in 允许几乎所有 type pair），\\n    能 enforce 的 DR reduction 空间有限，grammar 的 enabling 效应被 constraint looseness 稀释。\\nRV（~25%）和 ET（~6%）保持高位确认 semantic 无法替代 grammar 的 structural 功能—— 但这只证明 grammar 独立有用，不证明 grammar enables semantic。 Enabling dependency 退化为 \\\"grammar 独立有用 + semantic 独立有用\\\"，不再是 prerequisite 关系。\\n\"\n123\t  },\n124\t  {\n125\t    \"name\": \"DocRED tightness-DR Spearman correlation analysis\",\n126\t    \"description\": \"计算 DocRED 96 relations 的 constraint tightness（valid_pairs / all_possible_entity_type_pairs）与 full_s1 residual DR 的 Spearman rank correlation，验证 SciERC 的 tightness→high DR pattern 是否跨数据集复现。\",\n127\t    \"results\": {\n128\t      \"spearman_rho\": 0.14,\n129\t      \"spearman_p_value\": 0.18,\n130\t      \"direction\": \"positive but not significant\",\n131\t      \"per_rel_near_zero_fraction\": 0.38,\n132\t      \"relations_with_dr_above_10pct\": 28,\n133\t      \"relations_with_dr_zero\": 37,\n134\t      \"tight_relations_with_unexpectedly_low_dr\": 12,\n135\t      \"loose_relations_with_unexpectedly_high_dr\": 8,\n136\t      \"kendall_tau\": 0.1\n137\t    },\n138\t    \"tables\": [\n139\t      {\n140\t        \"name\": \"DocRED Tightness-DR by Quartile\",\n141\t        \"columns\": [\n142\t          \"Tightness_Quartile\",\n143\t          \"N_rels\",\n144\t          \"Median_Triples\",\n145\t          \"Mean_DR(%)\",\n146\t          \"Near_Zero_Frac\"\n147\t        ],\n148\t        \"rows\": [\n149\t          [\n150\t            \"Q1 (tightest)\",\n151\t            24,\n152\t            42,\n153\t            12.8,\n154\t            0.33\n155\t          ],\n156\t          [\n157\t            \"Q2\",\n158\t            24,\n159\t            85,\n160\t            9.5,\n161\t            0.42\n162\t          ],\n163\t          [\n164\t            \"Q3\",\n165\t            24,\n166\t            120,\n167\t            10.2,\n168\t            0.38\n169\t          ],\n170\t          [\n171\t            \"Q4 (loosest)\",\n172\t            24,\n173\t            210,\n174\t            8.9,\n175\t            0.42\n176\t          ]\n177\t        ]\n178\t      },\n179\t      {\n180\t        \"name\": \"Counter-examples to Tightness-DR Hypothesis\",\n181\t        \"columns\": [\n182\t          \"Relation\",\n183\t          \"Tightness\",\n184\t          \"Valid_Pairs\",\n185\t          \"Triples\",\n186\t          \"DR(%)\",\n187\t          \"Explanation\"\n188\t        ],\n189\t        \"rows\": [\n190\t          [\n191\t            \"P35_head_of_state\",\n192\t            \"tight\",\n193\t            2,\n194\t            45,\n195\t            2.2,\n196\t            \"Model prior aligns with constraint\"\n197\t          ],\n198\t          [\n199\t            \"P131_located_in\",\n200\t            \"loose\",\n201\t            15,\n202\t            580,\n203\t            14.8,\n204\t            \"LOC/ORG/MISC boundary confusion\"\n205\t          ],\n206\t          [\n207\t            \"P710_participant\",\n208\t            \"tight\",\n209\t            3,\n210\t            120,\n211\t            18.3,\n212\t            \"Model assigns diverse types to participants\"\n213\t          ],\n214\t          [\n215\t            \"P27_country_of_citizenship\",\n216\t            \"loose\",\n217\t            12,\n218\t            95,\n219\t            1.1,\n220\t            \"Citizenship prior strongly typed to PER→LOC\"\n221\t          ]\n222\t        ]\n223\t      }\n224\t    ],\n225\t    \"figures\": [],\n226\t    \"analysis\": \"Tightness-DR null result 是 worst tier 的 defining empirical finding。 Reframe 为 positive contribution： \\\"Constraint tightness predicts violation rate in small, well-defined ontologies (SciERC, ρ=0.85) but loses predictive power in complex ontologies (DocRED, ρ=0.14) where model priors, data frequency, and entity type granularity dominate.\\\" 这本身是有价值的 empirical observation，强化 violation landscape study 的 contribution。 但它同时意味着 semantic layer 无法用 tightness 来 prioritize enforcement—— 所有 relations 都需要 enforce，但 loose relations 上 enforcement 效果不佳。 §3 保留 SciERC tightness analysis，§5.4 报告 DocRED null result， §6 Discussion 将跨数据集对比作为 key finding。\\n\\n\\nSpearman ρ=0.14（p=0.18, not significant）：tightness-DR 在 DocRED 上无统计显著相关。原因： (a) 96 relations 中约 35 个有 <20 triples（低频），per-relation DR 的 sampling variance 极大\\n    （10 triples 中 1 个 violation 就是 10% DR），噪声淹没信号；\\n(b) DocRED 的 tightness 定义更模糊——many relations 的 ontology-defined domain/range 很宽\\n    （如 P131_located_in 允许 LOC→LOC, ORG→LOC, PER→LOC 等多种 pair），\\n    但实际数据分布高度集中在 1-2 种 pair，ontology tightness ≠ effective tightness；\\n(c) 部分 tight relations（P35_head_of_state, valid_pairs=2）DR 反而低，\\n    因为模型对 \\\"head of state\\\" 的 prior 恰好与约束一致（PER→LOC/ORG）；\\n    部分 loose relations（P131, valid_pairs=15）DR 反而高，\\n    因为模型的 location type assignment 在 ORG/LOC/MISC 之间不稳定。\\n38% 的 relations 达到 near-zero DR，但这些主要是低频 relations 且包含一些 inherently easy relations（如 P17_country, 模型 prior 与约束高度一致）， 不反映 method 的 systematic 成功。\\n\"\n227\t  },\n228\t  {\n229\t    \"name\": \"DocRED CF deep analysis\",\n230\t    \"description\": \"对 DocRED full_s1 的 519 cross-field consistency violations 做子类型分解（EVR/Within-rel）、per-relation 分布、entity type confusion pattern 分析，评估 semantic layer 在粗粒度 type system 上的副作用。\",\n231\t    \"results\": {\n232\t      \"cf_violations_total\": 519,\n233\t      \"cf_rate_per_triple\": 0.0299,\n234\t      \"cf_rate_per_entity\": 0.0257,\n235\t      \"evr_entities\": 380,\n236\t      \"evr_entity_rate\": 0.0188,\n237\t      \"within_rel_count\": 45,\n238\t      \"entity_duplication_instances\": 85,\n239\t      \"top_confusion_patterns\": [\n240\t        {\n241\t          \"pattern\": \"ORG↔LOC\",\n242\t          \"count\": 95,\n243\t          \"example\": \"'Washington' as ORG in P131 but LOC in P17\"\n244\t        },\n245\t        {\n246\t          \"pattern\": \"PER↔ORG\",\n247\t          \"count\": 72,\n248\t          \"example\": \"'Trump Organization' as PER in P35 but ORG in P127\"\n249\t        },\n250\t        {\n251\t          \"pattern\": \"MISC↔LOC\",\n252\t          \"count\": 48,\n253\t          \"example\": \"'European Union' as MISC in P463 but LOC in P131\"\n254\t        }\n255\t      ],\n256\t      \"cf_rate_broadened_definition\": 0.052,\n257\t      \"semantic_layer_induced_triple_increase_pct\": 7.2\n258\t    },\n259\t    \"tables\": [\n260\t      {\n261\t        \"name\": \"DocRED CF Sub-type Breakdown\",\n262\t        \"columns\": [\n263\t          \"Sub-type\",\n264\t          \"Count\",\n265\t          \"Rate(%)\",\n266\t          \"Severity\",\n267\t          \"SciERC_Comparable\"\n268\t        ],\n269\t        \"rows\": [\n270\t          [\n271\t            \"EVR (entity-vs-relation drift)\",\n272\t            380,\n273\t            1.88,\n274\t            \"Medium-High\",\n275\t            \"Yes (245/2474=7.34% on SciERC)\"\n276\t          ],\n277\t          [\n278\t            \"Within-rel inconsistency\",\n279\t            45,\n280\t            0.26,\n281\t            \"High\",\n282\t            \"Yes (10/2474=0.36% on SciERC)\"\n283\t          ],\n284\t          [\n285\t            \"Entity duplication (new)\",\n286\t            85,\n287\t            0.42,\n288\t            \"Medium\",\n289\t            \"Not observed on SciERC\"\n290\t          ],\n291\t          [\n292\t            \"Hallucinated extra triples\",\n293\t            \"~35\",\n294\t            0.2,\n295\t            \"High\",\n296\t            \"Not measured on SciERC\"\n297\t          ]\n298\t        ]\n299\t      },\n300\t      {\n301\t        \"name\": \"Top Entity Type Confusion Patterns\",\n302\t        \"columns\": [\n303\t          \"Pattern\",\n304\t          \"Count\",\n305\t          \"Hard_or_Soft_Boundary\"\n306\t        ],\n307\t        \"rows\": [\n308\t          [\n309\t            \"ORG↔LOC\",\n310\t            95,\n311\t            \"Soft (geopolitical entities)\"\n312\t          ],\n313\t          [\n314\t            \"PER↔ORG\",\n315\t            72,\n316\t            \"Hard (clear NER distinction)\"\n317\t          ],\n318\t          [\n319\t            \"MISC↔LOC\",\n320\t            48,\n321\t            \"Soft (political entities)\"\n322\t          ],\n323\t          [\n324\t            \"PER↔MISC\",\n325\t            28,\n326\t            \"Medium\"\n327\t          ]\n328\t        ]\n329\t      }\n330\t    ],\n331\t    \"figures\": [],\n332\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED CF 暴露两个 SciERC 上未出现的新问题（entity duplication + hallucinated triples）， 且 confusion pattern 更难 dismiss（PER↔ORG 是 hard boundary）。 论文防御策略升级： (1) 承认 DocRED CF 比 SciERC 更严重且性质不同； (2) 归因为 \\\"coarse-grained type system + per-relation independent enforcement 的交互效应\\\"； (3) Entity duplication 作为新发现的副作用专门报告（1-2 句 in §5.4）； (4) §7 Limitation 明确将 DocRED CF 列为 \\\"method does not scale gracefully to\\n    complex ontologies with coarse type systems\\\"。\\n这与 worst tier 的 narrative pivot 一致：semantic layer 是 proof-of-concept for tight ontologies。\\n\\n\\nDocRED CF analysis 在 worst tier 下暴露 semantic layer 在 coarse-grained type system 上的系统性问题： (a) EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）占 CF 的 ~73%（380/519），同一 entity\\n    在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋不同 type，与 SciERC 的 EVR 占比（>90%）一致，\\n    但 DocRED 的 PER/ORG/LOC/MISC 四类 boundary 比 SciERC 的 Generic/OtherScientificTerm 更 \\\"hard\\\"——\\n    PER vs ORG 在标准 NER 评估中是 clear error，不能轻易 dismiss 为 type ambiguity；\\n(b) Entity duplication（85 instances）：semantic layer 的 per-relation type enforcement\\n    迫使模型对同一 entity 在不同 relation context 中生成不同 type，\\n    有时这导致 entity 被重复生成（带不同 type label），\\n    inflating entity count（full_s1 20218 entities vs unconstrained ~19800, +2.1%）；\\n(c) 如果将 entity duplication 纳入广义 CF 定义，CF rate 从 2.99% 升至 ~5.2%，\\n    进入 worst tier 定义的 4-7% 范围；\\n(d) Semantic layer 的 constraint enforcement 在某些 relation 上迫使 model 选择次优 entity type，\\n    产生\\\"补偿性\\\"额外 triples（full_s1 17372 vs unconstrained ~16200, +7.2%），\\n    额外 triples 中约 3% 是 gold 中无对应的幻觉关系。\\nTop confusion patterns 集中在 DocRED coarse-grained type system 的固有模糊区， 但与 SciERC 不同的是，PER↔ORG 在 downstream application 中是 real error， reviewer 不太可能接受 \\\"type system ambiguity\\\" 的辩护。\\n\"\n333\t  },\n334\t  {\n335\t    \"name\": \"Latency comparison (constrained vs unconstrained)\",\n336\t    \"description\": \"测量 SciERC/DocRED 各 decoding mode 的 wall-clock latency，含 grammar compilation time 和 per-token inference overhead。使用与主实验相同的 GPU（RTX PRO 6000）和 batch_size=1。\",\n337\t    \"results\": {\n338\t      \"scierc_unconstrained_sec_per_sample\": 2.8,\n339\t      \"scierc_grammar_only_sec_per_sample\": 3.2,\n340\t      \"scierc_semantic_only_sec_per_sample\": 3.9,\n341\t      \"scierc_full_s1_sec_per_sample\": 4.3,\n342\t      \"scierc_full_s2_sec_per_sample\": 6.1,\n343\t      \"docred_unconstrained_sec_per_doc\": 18.5,\n344\t      \"docred_grammar_only_sec_per_doc\": 21.2,\n345\t      \"docred_full_s1_sec_per_doc\": 28.5,\n346\t      \"grammar_compilation_overhead_sec\": 0.8,\n347\t      \"overhead_grammar_pct\": 14.3,\n348\t      \"overhead_semantic_pct\": 39.3,\n349\t      \"overhead_full_s1_pct\": 53.6,\n350\t      \"overhead_full_s2_pct\": 117.9,\n351\t      \"tokens_per_second_unconstrained\": 42.5,\n352\t      \"tokens_per_second_full_s1\": 27.8\n353\t    },\n354\t    \"tables\": [\n355\t      {\n356\t        \"name\": \"Latency Comparison (SciERC)\",\n357\t        \"columns\": [\n358\t          \"Mode\",\n359\t          \"sec/sample\",\n360\t          \"Overhead(%)\",\n361\t          \"tok/s\"\n362\t        ],\n363\t        \"rows\": [\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"Unconstrained\",\n366\t            2.8,\n367\t            \"-\",\n368\t            42.5\n369\t          ],\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"Grammar-only\",\n372\t            3.2,\n373\t            14.3,\n374\t            37.2\n375\t          ],\n376\t          [\n377\t            \"Semantic-only\",\n378\t            3.9,\n379\t            39.3,\n380\t            30.5\n381\t          ],\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"Full S1\",\n384\t            4.3,\n385\t            53.6,\n386\t            27.8\n387\t          ],\n388\t          [\n389\t            \"Full S2\",\n390\t            6.1,\n391\t            117.9,\n392\t            19.5\n393\t          ]\n394\t        ]\n395\t      },\n396\t      {\n397\t        \"name\": \"Latency Comparison (DocRED)\",\n398\t        \"columns\": [\n399\t          \"Mode\",\n400\t          \"sec/doc\",\n401\t          \"Overhead(%)\",\n402\t          \"Total_hours(998 docs)\"\n403\t        ],\n404\t        \"rows\": [\n405\t          [\n406\t            \"Unconstrained\",\n407\t            18.5,\n408\t            \"-\",\n409\t            5.1\n410\t          ],\n411\t          [\n412\t            \"Grammar-only\",\n413\t            21.2,\n414\t            14.6,\n415\t            5.9\n416\t          ],\n417\t          [\n418\t            \"Full S1\",\n419\t            28.5,\n420\t            54.1,\n421\t            7.9\n422\t          ]\n423\t        ]\n424\t      }\n425\t    ],\n426\t    \"figures\": [],\n427\t    \"analysis\": \"Latency 在 worst tier 下非论文主要风险。54% overhead 可 defend 为 \\\"sub-2x cost for near-elimination of structural violations\\\"。 但需注意两个 reviewer 攻击面： (a) Post-hoc filtering overhead ≈ 0%，latency argument 对 post-hoc 不利；\\n    rebuttal: post-hoc 无法 redirect probability mass，只能丢弃（~16% waste on DocRED）；\\n(b) S2 的 >2x overhead + 无 metric improvement 进一步支持降级为 appendix。 建议 §5 用 1 段报告 latency，不做独立 subsection。 Overhead 归因到 Python-level mask computation 暗示 C++/CUDA 优化可降至 <20%—— 可在 §7 Future Work 中提及但不 overclaim。\\n\\n\\nGrammar layer（XGrammar）overhead ~14%，较小，因为 XGrammar 使用预编译 FSM， per-token masking 是 O(vocab_size) 位操作且在 GPU 上高效并行。 Semantic layer overhead ~39%，显著更大： (a) 每个 relation triple 的 head/tail type position 需要查询 entity registry（Python dict lookup），\\n    DocRED 的 registry 随 document entities 增长，per-query 时间非 O(1)；\\n(b) dynamic logit masking 在每个 type token position 需要 enumerate valid types for current relation，\\n    DocRED 96 relations 的 lookup table 远大于 SciERC 7 relations；\\n(c) Python-level 的 mask computation 是 bottleneck（非 GPU kernel），\\n    batch_size=1 意味着 CPU-GPU 交替频繁。\\nFull S1 = grammar + semantic combined，overhead 不是简单相加（14+39=53%） 因为两个 mask 的 bitwise AND 本身几乎 zero cost。实测 ~54% 合理。 Full S2 overhead ~118% 因为两次 full inference + 中间 entity extraction + grammar recompilation， 在 DocRED 上 per-doc 会更夸张（~55 sec vs 18.5 sec unconstrained, ~200% overhead）。 54% overhead 对 zero-shot extraction 可接受，但 reviewer 可能与 post-hoc filtering（~0% overhead）对比。\\n\"\n428\t  },\n429\t  {\n430\t    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B violation rate (SciERC minimal)\",\n431\t    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct 在 SciERC 上运行 minimal prompt（与 Qwen3-8B Phase 0 P001 相同设置），验证 violation landscape 的跨模型泛化性。Stretch goal，仅在 GPU 时间充裕时执行。\",\n432\t    \"results\": {\n433\t      \"total_triples\": 1580,\n434\t      \"total_entities\": 2350,\n435\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.92,\n436\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.012,\n437\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.035,\n438\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.098,\n439\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.002,\n440\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.065,\n441\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.275,\n442\t      \"per_relation_dr\": {\n443\t        \"Used-for\": 0.005,\n444\t        \"Feature-of\": 0.18,\n445\t        \"Compare\": 0.31,\n446\t        \"Evaluate-for\": 0.19,\n447\t        \"Hyponym-of\": 0.11,\n448\t        \"Part-of\": 0.15,\n449\t        \"Conjunction\": 0.01\n450\t      },\n451\t      \"per_relation_rank_correlation_vs_qwen\": 0.82\n452\t    },\n453\t    \"tables\": [\n454\t      {\n455\t        \"name\": \"Cross-Model Violation Comparison (SciERC)\",\n456\t        \"columns\": [\n457\t          \"Model\",\n458\t          \"DR(%)\",\n459\t          \"RV(%)\",\n460\t          \"ET(%)\",\n461\t          \"Parse(%)\",\n462\t          \"R-F1(%)\",\n463\t          \"Triples\"\n464\t        ],\n465\t        \"rows\": [\n466\t          [\n467\t            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n468\t            15.4,\n469\t            1.39,\n470\t            0.4,\n471\t            100,\n472\t            8.23,\n473\t            1724\n474\t          ],\n475\t          [\n476\t            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n477\t            9.8,\n478\t            3.5,\n479\t            1.2,\n480\t            92,\n481\t            6.5,\n482\t            1580\n483\t          ]\n484\t        ]\n485\t      },\n486\t      {\n487\t        \"name\": \"Per-Relation DR Rank Comparison\",\n488\t        \"columns\": [\n489\t          \"Relation\",\n490\t          \"Qwen_DR(%)\",\n491\t          \"Qwen_Rank\",\n492\t          \"Llama_DR(%)\",\n493\t          \"Llama_Rank\"\n494\t        ],\n495\t        \"rows\": [\n496\t          [\n497\t            \"Compare\",\n498\t            42.4,\n499\t            1,\n500\t            31.0,\n501\t            1\n502\t          ],\n503\t          [\n504\t            \"Feature-of\",\n505\t            33.5,\n506\t            2,\n507\t            18.0,\n508\t            3\n509\t          ],\n510\t          [\n511\t            \"Part-of\",\n512\t            25.0,\n513\t            3,\n514\t            15.0,\n515\t            4\n516\t          ],\n517\t          [\n518\t            \"Evaluate-for\",\n519\t            24.1,\n520\t            4,\n521\t            19.0,\n522\t            2\n523\t          ],\n524\t          [\n525\t            \"Hyponym-of\",\n526\t            14.5,\n527\t            5,\n528\t            11.0,\n529\t            5\n530\t          ],\n531\t          [\n532\t            \"Used-for\",\n533\t            0.76,\n534\t            6,\n535\t            0.5,\n536\t            6\n537\t          ],\n538\t          [\n539\t            \"Conjunction\",\n540\t            0.0,\n541\t            7,\n542\t            1.0,\n543\t            7\n544\t          ]\n545\t        ]\n546\t      }\n547\t    ],\n548\t    \"figures\": [],\n549\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model 在 worst tier 下是 mixed signal： Pro: per-relation rank order 保持（ρ=0.82），支持 \\\"violation landscape structure is model-agnostic\\\"； Con: absolute DR 差异大（9.8% vs 15.4%），reviewer 可 argue \\\"problem severity is model-specific， 换个 model 可能根本不需要 constrained decoding\\\"。 更大的 con: Llama 的 92% parse rate 使对比不 clean——unparseable output 的 violation 未计入。 Worst tier 建议：如果 GPU 时间紧张（May 17 前），skip P012 更安全。 Ambiguous cross-model results 给 reviewer 额外攻击面，而 single-model limitation 已经在 §7 中 proactively disclosed——running P012 只在结果 clean 时才有 upside， 在 worst tier 下大概率是 downside（need to explain parse rate confound + absolute rate gap）。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.1-8B 预期 baseline DR=9.8%，低于 Qwen3-8B 的 15.4%，原因： (a) Llama 系列 instruction tuning 更偏向 structured output compliance，\\n    对 domain/range 约束的隐式 adherence 优于 Qwen（Meta 的 RLHF 更强调 format following）；\\n(b) Llama tokenizer 对 SciERC entity type names 的分词差异（BPE 不同）\\n    可能使某些 type names 在 generation 中被更自然地产生；\\n(c) Llama 的 pretraining corpus 可能包含更多 structured extraction examples（Code Llama lineage）。 但 json_parse_rate=92% 引入 confound：Llama 生成更多 unparseable JSON（8% failure rate）， 这些 failure 中可能包含大量 would-have-been violations， 使得 DR=9.8% 可能是 survivorship bias（只测量了能 parse 的 92%， 另外 8% 的 violation rate 未知）。 低 R-F1（6.5% vs Qwen 8.2%）同向支持：Llama 在 SciERC IE 上整体弱于 Qwen， 生成的 triples 更少且更保守，violation rate 低可能是 \\\"生成少 → 违反少\\\" 而非 \\\"更遵守约束\\\"。 Per-relation rank correlation 与 Qwen 约 0.82（Compare/Feature-of 仍是 top violators）， 说明 violation landscape 的 relative pattern 跨模型保持，但 absolute rates model-dependent。\\n\"\n550\t  },\n551\t  {\n552\t    \"name\": \"DocRED full S2 two-pass constrained decoding\",\n553\t    \"description\": \"在 DocRED 上运行 S2：Pass 1 grammar-only entity extraction，Pass 2 基于 Pass 1 entities 编译 input-dependent grammar 后 relation extraction。验证 S2 在 96-relation ontology 上的表现。\",\n554\t    \"results\": {\n555\t      \"documents_checked\": 978,\n556\t      \"total_triples\": 16800,\n557\t      \"total_entities\": 19500,\n558\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.108,\n559\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n560\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n561\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.048,\n562\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0798,\n563\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.582,\n564\t      \"latency_overhead_vs_unconstrained_pct\": 135,\n565\t      \"dr_delta_vs_s1_pp\": 0.61\n566\t    },\n567\t    \"tables\": [\n568\t      {\n569\t        \"name\": \"S1 vs S2 Cross-Dataset Summary\",\n570\t        \"columns\": [\n571\t          \"Dataset\",\n572\t          \"S1_DR(%)\",\n573\t          \"S2_DR(%)\",\n574\t          \"S1_CF(%)\",\n575\t          \"S2_CF(%)\",\n576\t          \"S1_RF1(%)\",\n577\t          \"S2_RF1(%)\"\n578\t        ],\n579\t        \"rows\": [\n580\t          [\n581\t            \"SciERC\",\n582\t            0.93,\n583\t            0.97,\n584\t            9.9,\n585\t            8.03,\n586\t            8.36,\n587\t            8.03\n588\t          ],\n589\t          [\n590\t            \"DocRED (predicted)\",\n591\t            10.19,\n592\t            10.8,\n593\t            2.99,\n594\t            4.8,\n595\t            8.17,\n596\t            7.98\n597\t          ]\n598\t        ]\n599\t      }\n600\t    ],\n601\t    \"figures\": [],\n602\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED S2 的预期负面结果强化 \\\"S2 降为 appendix\\\" 的决策。 在 worst tier 下建议完全跳过——GPU 时间优先保障 DocRED unconstrained rerun 和 semantic_only（这两个是消融表 + enabling ratio 的必需数据）， S2 on DocRED 的 expected negative result 只增加论文中需要解释的 noise。 论文中处理为 \\\"S2 results on SciERC (Appendix A) show comparable performance to S1; we leave cross-dataset S2 evaluation to future work.\\\"\\n\\nS2 在 SciERC 上已确认无优势（DR 0.97% ≈ S1 0.93%，CF 8.03% ≈ S1 9.9%）。 DocRED 上预期同样无优势，原因： (a) S2 的 Pass 1 entity extraction 在 DocRED 上 error propagation 更严重——\\n    96 relations 意味着 Pass 2 的 input-dependent grammar 需要涵盖更多 relation type 的 constraints，\\n    Pass 1 的任何 entity type error 都会导致 Pass 2 constraint set 偏差；\\n(b) DocRED document 长度大（avg ~200 words），两次 full inference 的 token 总量翻倍，\\n    但 constraint quality 不提升；\\n(c) DR=10.8%（vs S1 10.19%）略差，因为 Pass 1 entity errors propagate：\\n    Pass 1 将 entity X 标注为 ORG，Pass 2 grammar 据此编译 ORG-compatible relations，\\n    但 X 实际是 LOC，导致 Pass 2 在 X 参与的 triples 上 enforce 了错误的 constraints；\\n(d) CF=4.8% 高于 S1 的 2.99%，因为 S2 的 entity registry 基于 Pass 1 output，\\n    而 Pass 2 的 relation extraction 可能 assign 不同 type（两个 pass 各自独立推理 type），\\n    within-pass consistency 比 single-pass 更难保证。\\n在 worst tier 下强烈建议不运行此实验——节省 ~16 GPU-hours 用于论文写作。 SciERC S2 data 已足够支持 \\\"S2 is architectural variant, not improvement\\\" 的 conclusion。\\n\"\n603\t  }\n604\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ebf8474-508b-47ef-8b53-5e664546d2e0","uuid":"fb615c8d-5853-4a18-977a-bb49fdca0017","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:37:21.618Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T094226/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 Phase 2 pipeline 重跑 DocRED unconstrained，与 constrained 实验共用相同 prompt/generation config/post-processing，确保消融表 F1/violation 对比公平。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents_checked\": 975,\n      \"parse_failures\": 23,\n      \"total_entities\": 19800,\n      \"total_triples\": 16200,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.068,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.265,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.158,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0808,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.585,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.977,\n      \"dr_reduction_vs_full_s1_pct\": 35.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 Full Ablation Table\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Mode\",\n          \"DR(%)\",\n          \"RV(%)\",\n          \"ET(%)\",\n          \"CF(%)\",\n          \"R-F1\",\n          \"Triples\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Unconstrained\",\n            15.8,\n            26.5,\n            6.8,\n            0.1,\n            8.08,\n            16200\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Grammar-only\",\n            26.17,\n            0.03,\n            0.0,\n            0.08,\n            8.24,\n            17341\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Semantic-only\",\n            11.2,\n            24.8,\n            5.9,\n            3.8,\n            7.95,\n            16050\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full S1\",\n            10.19,\n            0.03,\n            0.0,\n            2.99,\n            8.17,\n            17372\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DR reduction 35.5% 远低于 SciERC 94%，直接挑战 cross-dataset generalization claim。 Grammar-only DR=26.17% > unconstrained DR=15.8% 的现象需要 §5.4 专门解释： grammar 消除 ~27% 的 RV violations 后，原先有 invalid relation name 的 triples 现在有了 valid relation name，可以被 DR checker 评估，暴露大量新 DR violations。 这不是 grammar 变差了，而是 Phase 0 的 DR=18.7% 本身就低估了（被 RV 掩盖了真实 DR）。 如果用 grammar-only 26.17% 作为 \\\"真实 baseline\\\"， full_s1 的 DR reduction = (26.17-10.19)/26.17 = 61.1%——但这个 framing 有 cherry-picking 嫌疑。 论文需要同时报告两个 baseline 的 reduction%，让 reader 自行判断。\\n\\n\\nPhase 2 code path 使用统一 prompt template（含 JSON schema instruction）和 generation config （temperature=0.6, top_p=0.95, thinking mode /no_think），与 Phase 0 minimal prompt 存在细微差异。 预期 DR 从 Phase 0 的 18.7% 降至 ~15.8%，原因三重： (a) Phase 2 统一 JSON instruction 隐式提供了更清晰的 type 格式指导，\\n    模型对 domain/range 的 implicit adherence 轻微提升；\\n(b) Phase 0 使用 raw minimal prompt，Phase 2 code path 的 prompt wrapper 结构更整洁，\\n    部分 Phase 0 边界 case 在 Phase 2 中被分类为 parse failure（23 failures vs Phase 0 的 36 failures），\\n    denominator 缩小使 DR 的百分比下降；\\n(c) generation config 的差异（max_new_tokens=4096 统一设定 vs Phase 0 可能不同）\\n    影响长文档的 truncation behavior，改变 tail triples 的 violation 分布。\\nDR=15.8% 使 full_s1 的 DR reduction 仅为 (15.8-10.19)/15.8 = 35.5%， 远低于 SciERC 的 94%（0.93/15.37）和 Phase 0 基线计算的 45.5%（10.19/18.7）。 这是 worst tier 的核心数字痛点：fair-comparison baseline 偏低导致 improvement narrative 被压缩。 RV/ET 保持 Phase 0 水平（~27%/~7%），因为无 grammar 约束。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED Phase 2 semantic-only constrained decoding\",\n    \"description\": \"仅启用 semantic layer（TypeConstraintProcessor），不启用 grammar layer（XGrammar），验证 grammar enabling dependency 是否在复杂 ontology 上复现。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents_checked\": 970,\n      \"total_triples\": 16050,\n      \"total_entities\": 19600,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.059,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.248,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.112,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.038,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0795,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.58,\n      \"semantic_enabling_ratio\": 1.1,\n      \"semantic_dr_reduction_vs_unconstrained_pct\": 29.1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Enabling Dependency Cross-Dataset Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Dataset\",\n          \"Ontology_Size\",\n          \"semantic_only_DR(%)\",\n          \"full_s1_DR(%)\",\n          \"Enabling_Ratio\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SciERC\",\n            \"7 rels\",\n            11.65,\n            0.93,\n            12.5,\n            \"Strong enabling: grammar prerequisite\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DocRED\",\n            \"96 rels\",\n            11.2,\n            10.19,\n            1.1,\n            \"No enabling: layers independent\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Enabling ratio=1.1 摧毁 Claim 3 的 composable with enabling dependency 叙事。 Reframe 策略：grammar 和 semantic 是两个独立 constraint layer， 各自解决不同 violation type（grammar→ET/RV 100% elimination, semantic→partial DR reduction）， 在 tight ontology 上 grammar 是 semantic 的 prerequisite（SciERC，12.5x）， 在 loose ontology 上两者 independently contribute（DocRED，1.1x）。 论文放弃 \\\"enabling dependency\\\" 作为 universal mechanism， 改为 \\\"enabling relationship modulated by constraint tightness and ontology vocabulary design\\\"。 这个 reframe 将 enabling ratio 的跨数据集差异转化为 empirical finding 而非 method failure。\\n\\n\\nWorst tier 核心预测：semantic_only DR ≈ 11.2%，full_s1 DR = 10.19%， enabling ratio = 11.2/10.19 = 1.10。对比 SciERC enabling ratio = 11.65/0.93 = 12.5。 Grammar 对 semantic 的 enabling 在 DocRED 上几乎不存在，原因三层： (a) DocRED 使用 Wikidata property ID（P31, P17, P131 等短 ID），\\n    模型生成 invalid relation name 后，这些 ID 仍有较高概率恰好是某个 valid relation\\n    （96 relations 覆盖了大量常见 Pxxx pattern），\\n    因此 semantic layer 在无 grammar 时仍能对多数 triples 做 constraint lookup；\\n(b) SciERC 使用自然语言 relation name（\\\"Used-for\\\", \\\"Feature-of\\\"），\\n    无 grammar 时 RV violation 率高（1.51%），这些 triples 的 relation 不在 ontology 中，\\n    semantic layer 直接 skip，无法 enforce DR constraint——这才是 enabling 的来源；\\n(c) DocRED semantic layer 的 per-relation constraints 本身宽松（avg 5.68 valid pairs，\\n    但高频 relations 如 P131_located_in 允许几乎所有 type pair），\\n    能 enforce 的 DR reduction 空间有限，grammar 的 enabling 效应被 constraint looseness 稀释。\\nRV（~25%）和 ET（~6%）保持高位确认 semantic 无法替代 grammar 的 structural 功能—— 但这只证明 grammar 独立有用，不证明 grammar enables semantic。 Enabling dependency 退化为 \\\"grammar 独立有用 + semantic 独立有用\\\"，不再是 prerequisite 关系。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED tightness-DR Spearman correlation analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"计算 DocRED 96 relations 的 constraint tightness（valid_pairs / all_possible_entity_type_pairs）与 full_s1 residual DR 的 Spearman rank correlation，验证 SciERC 的 tightness→high DR pattern 是否跨数据集复现。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"spearman_rho\": 0.14,\n      \"spearman_p_value\": 0.18,\n      \"direction\": \"positive but not significant\",\n      \"per_rel_near_zero_fraction\": 0.38,\n      \"relations_with_dr_above_10pct\": 28,\n      \"relations_with_dr_zero\": 37,\n      \"tight_relations_with_unexpectedly_low_dr\": 12,\n      \"loose_relations_with_unexpectedly_high_dr\": 8,\n      \"kendall_tau\": 0.1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"DocRED Tightness-DR by Quartile\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Tightness_Quartile\",\n          \"N_rels\",\n          \"Median_Triples\",\n          \"Mean_DR(%)\",\n          \"Near_Zero_Frac\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Q1 (tightest)\",\n            24,\n            42,\n            12.8,\n            0.33\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Q2\",\n            24,\n            85,\n            9.5,\n            0.42\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Q3\",\n            24,\n            120,\n            10.2,\n            0.38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Q4 (loosest)\",\n            24,\n            210,\n            8.9,\n            0.42\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Counter-examples to Tightness-DR Hypothesis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Relation\",\n          \"Tightness\",\n          \"Valid_Pairs\",\n          \"Triples\",\n          \"DR(%)\",\n          \"Explanation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"P35_head_of_state\",\n            \"tight\",\n            2,\n            45,\n            2.2,\n            \"Model prior aligns with constraint\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"P131_located_in\",\n            \"loose\",\n            15,\n            580,\n            14.8,\n            \"LOC/ORG/MISC boundary confusion\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"P710_participant\",\n            \"tight\",\n            3,\n            120,\n            18.3,\n            \"Model assigns diverse types to participants\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"P27_country_of_citizenship\",\n            \"loose\",\n            12,\n            95,\n            1.1,\n            \"Citizenship prior strongly typed to PER→LOC\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Tightness-DR null result 是 worst tier 的 defining empirical finding。 Reframe 为 positive contribution： \\\"Constraint tightness predicts violation rate in small, well-defined ontologies (SciERC, ρ=0.85) but loses predictive power in complex ontologies (DocRED, ρ=0.14) where model priors, data frequency, and entity type granularity dominate.\\\" 这本身是有价值的 empirical observation，强化 violation landscape study 的 contribution。 但它同时意味着 semantic layer 无法用 tightness 来 prioritize enforcement—— 所有 relations 都需要 enforce，但 loose relations 上 enforcement 效果不佳。 §3 保留 SciERC tightness analysis，§5.4 报告 DocRED null result， §6 Discussion 将跨数据集对比作为 key finding。\\n\\n\\nSpearman ρ=0.14（p=0.18, not significant）：tightness-DR 在 DocRED 上无统计显著相关。原因： (a) 96 relations 中约 35 个有 <20 triples（低频），per-relation DR 的 sampling variance 极大\\n    （10 triples 中 1 个 violation 就是 10% DR），噪声淹没信号；\\n(b) DocRED 的 tightness 定义更模糊——many relations 的 ontology-defined domain/range 很宽\\n    （如 P131_located_in 允许 LOC→LOC, ORG→LOC, PER→LOC 等多种 pair），\\n    但实际数据分布高度集中在 1-2 种 pair，ontology tightness ≠ effective tightness；\\n(c) 部分 tight relations（P35_head_of_state, valid_pairs=2）DR 反而低，\\n    因为模型对 \\\"head of state\\\" 的 prior 恰好与约束一致（PER→LOC/ORG）；\\n    部分 loose relations（P131, valid_pairs=15）DR 反而高，\\n    因为模型的 location type assignment 在 ORG/LOC/MISC 之间不稳定。\\n38% 的 relations 达到 near-zero DR，但这些主要是低频 relations 且包含一些 inherently easy relations（如 P17_country, 模型 prior 与约束高度一致）， 不反映 method 的 systematic 成功。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED CF deep analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"对 DocRED full_s1 的 519 cross-field consistency violations 做子类型分解（EVR/Within-rel）、per-relation 分布、entity type confusion pattern 分析，评估 semantic layer 在粗粒度 type system 上的副作用。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cf_violations_total\": 519,\n      \"cf_rate_per_triple\": 0.0299,\n      \"cf_rate_per_entity\": 0.0257,\n      \"evr_entities\": 380,\n      \"evr_entity_rate\": 0.0188,\n      \"within_rel_count\": 45,\n      \"entity_duplication_instances\": 85,\n      \"top_confusion_patterns\": [\n        {\n          \"pattern\": \"ORG↔LOC\",\n          \"count\": 95,\n          \"example\": \"'Washington' as ORG in P131 but LOC in P17\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"pattern\": \"PER↔ORG\",\n          \"count\": 72,\n          \"example\": \"'Trump Organization' as PER in P35 but ORG in P127\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"pattern\": \"MISC↔LOC\",\n          \"count\": 48,\n          \"example\": \"'European Union' as MISC in P463 but LOC in P131\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cf_rate_broadened_definition\": 0.052,\n      \"semantic_layer_induced_triple_increase_pct\": 7.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"DocRED CF Sub-type Breakdown\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Sub-type\",\n          \"Count\",\n          \"Rate(%)\",\n          \"Severity\",\n          \"SciERC_Comparable\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"EVR (entity-vs-relation drift)\",\n            380,\n            1.88,\n            \"Medium-High\",\n            \"Yes (245/2474=7.34% on SciERC)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Within-rel inconsistency\",\n            45,\n            0.26,\n            \"High\",\n            \"Yes (10/2474=0.36% on SciERC)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Entity duplication (new)\",\n            85,\n            0.42,\n            \"Medium\",\n            \"Not observed on SciERC\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Hallucinated extra triples\",\n            \"~35\",\n            0.2,\n            \"High\",\n            \"Not measured on SciERC\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Top Entity Type Confusion Patterns\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Pattern\",\n          \"Count\",\n          \"Hard_or_Soft_Boundary\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ORG↔LOC\",\n            95,\n            \"Soft (geopolitical entities)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"PER↔ORG\",\n            72,\n            \"Hard (clear NER distinction)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MISC↔LOC\",\n            48,\n            \"Soft (political entities)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"PER↔MISC\",\n            28,\n            \"Medium\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED CF 暴露两个 SciERC 上未出现的新问题（entity duplication + hallucinated triples）， 且 confusion pattern 更难 dismiss（PER↔ORG 是 hard boundary）。 论文防御策略升级： (1) 承认 DocRED CF 比 SciERC 更严重且性质不同； (2) 归因为 \\\"coarse-grained type system + per-relation independent enforcement 的交互效应\\\"； (3) Entity duplication 作为新发现的副作用专门报告（1-2 句 in §5.4）； (4) §7 Limitation 明确将 DocRED CF 列为 \\\"method does not scale gracefully to\\n    complex ontologies with coarse type systems\\\"。\\n这与 worst tier 的 narrative pivot 一致：semantic layer 是 proof-of-concept for tight ontologies。\\n\\n\\nDocRED CF analysis 在 worst tier 下暴露 semantic layer 在 coarse-grained type system 上的系统性问题： (a) EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）占 CF 的 ~73%（380/519），同一 entity\\n    在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋不同 type，与 SciERC 的 EVR 占比（>90%）一致，\\n    但 DocRED 的 PER/ORG/LOC/MISC 四类 boundary 比 SciERC 的 Generic/OtherScientificTerm 更 \\\"hard\\\"——\\n    PER vs ORG 在标准 NER 评估中是 clear error，不能轻易 dismiss 为 type ambiguity；\\n(b) Entity duplication（85 instances）：semantic layer 的 per-relation type enforcement\\n    迫使模型对同一 entity 在不同 relation context 中生成不同 type，\\n    有时这导致 entity 被重复生成（带不同 type label），\\n    inflating entity count（full_s1 20218 entities vs unconstrained ~19800, +2.1%）；\\n(c) 如果将 entity duplication 纳入广义 CF 定义，CF rate 从 2.99% 升至 ~5.2%，\\n    进入 worst tier 定义的 4-7% 范围；\\n(d) Semantic layer 的 constraint enforcement 在某些 relation 上迫使 model 选择次优 entity type，\\n    产生\\\"补偿性\\\"额外 triples（full_s1 17372 vs unconstrained ~16200, +7.2%），\\n    额外 triples 中约 3% 是 gold 中无对应的幻觉关系。\\nTop confusion patterns 集中在 DocRED coarse-grained type system 的固有模糊区， 但与 SciERC 不同的是，PER↔ORG 在 downstream application 中是 real error， reviewer 不太可能接受 \\\"type system ambiguity\\\" 的辩护。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Latency comparison (constrained vs unconstrained)\",\n    \"description\": \"测量 SciERC/DocRED 各 decoding mode 的 wall-clock latency，含 grammar compilation time 和 per-token inference overhead。使用与主实验相同的 GPU（RTX PRO 6000）和 batch_size=1。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scierc_unconstrained_sec_per_sample\": 2.8,\n      \"scierc_grammar_only_sec_per_sample\": 3.2,\n      \"scierc_semantic_only_sec_per_sample\": 3.9,\n      \"scierc_full_s1_sec_per_sample\": 4.3,\n      \"scierc_full_s2_sec_per_sample\": 6.1,\n      \"docred_unconstrained_sec_per_doc\": 18.5,\n      \"docred_grammar_only_sec_per_doc\": 21.2,\n      \"docred_full_s1_sec_per_doc\": 28.5,\n      \"grammar_compilation_overhead_sec\": 0.8,\n      \"overhead_grammar_pct\": 14.3,\n      \"overhead_semantic_pct\": 39.3,\n      \"overhead_full_s1_pct\": 53.6,\n      \"overhead_full_s2_pct\": 117.9,\n      \"tokens_per_second_unconstrained\": 42.5,\n      \"tokens_per_second_full_s1\": 27.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Latency Comparison (SciERC)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Mode\",\n          \"sec/sample\",\n          \"Overhead(%)\",\n          \"tok/s\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Unconstrained\",\n            2.8,\n            \"-\",\n            42.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Grammar-only\",\n            3.2,\n            14.3,\n            37.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Semantic-only\",\n            3.9,\n            39.3,\n            30.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full S1\",\n            4.3,\n            53.6,\n            27.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full S2\",\n            6.1,\n            117.9,\n            19.5\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Latency Comparison (DocRED)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Mode\",\n          \"sec/doc\",\n          \"Overhead(%)\",\n          \"Total_hours(998 docs)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Unconstrained\",\n            18.5,\n            \"-\",\n            5.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Grammar-only\",\n            21.2,\n            14.6,\n            5.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Full S1\",\n            28.5,\n            54.1,\n            7.9\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Latency 在 worst tier 下非论文主要风险。54% overhead 可 defend 为 \\\"sub-2x cost for near-elimination of structural violations\\\"。 但需注意两个 reviewer 攻击面： (a) Post-hoc filtering overhead ≈ 0%，latency argument 对 post-hoc 不利；\\n    rebuttal: post-hoc 无法 redirect probability mass，只能丢弃（~16% waste on DocRED）；\\n(b) S2 的 >2x overhead + 无 metric improvement 进一步支持降级为 appendix。 建议 §5 用 1 段报告 latency，不做独立 subsection。 Overhead 归因到 Python-level mask computation 暗示 C++/CUDA 优化可降至 <20%—— 可在 §7 Future Work 中提及但不 overclaim。\\n\\n\\nGrammar layer（XGrammar）overhead ~14%，较小，因为 XGrammar 使用预编译 FSM， per-token masking 是 O(vocab_size) 位操作且在 GPU 上高效并行。 Semantic layer overhead ~39%，显著更大： (a) 每个 relation triple 的 head/tail type position 需要查询 entity registry（Python dict lookup），\\n    DocRED 的 registry 随 document entities 增长，per-query 时间非 O(1)；\\n(b) dynamic logit masking 在每个 type token position 需要 enumerate valid types for current relation，\\n    DocRED 96 relations 的 lookup table 远大于 SciERC 7 relations；\\n(c) Python-level 的 mask computation 是 bottleneck（非 GPU kernel），\\n    batch_size=1 意味着 CPU-GPU 交替频繁。\\nFull S1 = grammar + semantic combined，overhead 不是简单相加（14+39=53%） 因为两个 mask 的 bitwise AND 本身几乎 zero cost。实测 ~54% 合理。 Full S2 overhead ~118% 因为两次 full inference + 中间 entity extraction + grammar recompilation， 在 DocRED 上 per-doc 会更夸张（~55 sec vs 18.5 sec unconstrained, ~200% overhead）。 54% overhead 对 zero-shot extraction 可接受，但 reviewer 可能与 post-hoc filtering（~0% overhead）对比。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B violation rate (SciERC minimal)\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct 在 SciERC 上运行 minimal prompt（与 Qwen3-8B Phase 0 P001 相同设置），验证 violation landscape 的跨模型泛化性。Stretch goal，仅在 GPU 时间充裕时执行。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 1580,\n      \"total_entities\": 2350,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.92,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.012,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.035,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.098,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.002,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.065,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.275,\n      \"per_relation_dr\": {\n        \"Used-for\": 0.005,\n        \"Feature-of\": 0.18,\n        \"Compare\": 0.31,\n        \"Evaluate-for\": 0.19,\n        \"Hyponym-of\": 0.11,\n        \"Part-of\": 0.15,\n        \"Conjunction\": 0.01\n      },\n      \"per_relation_rank_correlation_vs_qwen\": 0.82\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-Model Violation Comparison (SciERC)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"DR(%)\",\n          \"RV(%)\",\n          \"ET(%)\",\n          \"Parse(%)\",\n          \"R-F1(%)\",\n          \"Triples\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n            15.4,\n            1.39,\n            0.4,\n            100,\n            8.23,\n            1724\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            9.8,\n            3.5,\n            1.2,\n            92,\n            6.5,\n            1580\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Per-Relation DR Rank Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Relation\",\n          \"Qwen_DR(%)\",\n          \"Qwen_Rank\",\n          \"Llama_DR(%)\",\n          \"Llama_Rank\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Compare\",\n            42.4,\n            1,\n            31.0,\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Feature-of\",\n            33.5,\n            2,\n            18.0,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Part-of\",\n            25.0,\n            3,\n            15.0,\n            4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Evaluate-for\",\n            24.1,\n            4,\n            19.0,\n            2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Hyponym-of\",\n            14.5,\n            5,\n            11.0,\n            5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Used-for\",\n            0.76,\n            6,\n            0.5,\n            6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Conjunction\",\n            0.0,\n            7,\n            1.0,\n            7\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model 在 worst tier 下是 mixed signal： Pro: per-relation rank order 保持（ρ=0.82），支持 \\\"violation landscape structure is model-agnostic\\\"； Con: absolute DR 差异大（9.8% vs 15.4%），reviewer 可 argue \\\"problem severity is model-specific， 换个 model 可能根本不需要 constrained decoding\\\"。 更大的 con: Llama 的 92% parse rate 使对比不 clean——unparseable output 的 violation 未计入。 Worst tier 建议：如果 GPU 时间紧张（May 17 前），skip P012 更安全。 Ambiguous cross-model results 给 reviewer 额外攻击面，而 single-model limitation 已经在 §7 中 proactively disclosed——running P012 只在结果 clean 时才有 upside， 在 worst tier 下大概率是 downside（need to explain parse rate confound + absolute rate gap）。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.1-8B 预期 baseline DR=9.8%，低于 Qwen3-8B 的 15.4%，原因： (a) Llama 系列 instruction tuning 更偏向 structured output compliance，\\n    对 domain/range 约束的隐式 adherence 优于 Qwen（Meta 的 RLHF 更强调 format following）；\\n(b) Llama tokenizer 对 SciERC entity type names 的分词差异（BPE 不同）\\n    可能使某些 type names 在 generation 中被更自然地产生；\\n(c) Llama 的 pretraining corpus 可能包含更多 structured extraction examples（Code Llama lineage）。 但 json_parse_rate=92% 引入 confound：Llama 生成更多 unparseable JSON（8% failure rate）， 这些 failure 中可能包含大量 would-have-been violations， 使得 DR=9.8% 可能是 survivorship bias（只测量了能 parse 的 92%， 另外 8% 的 violation rate 未知）。 低 R-F1（6.5% vs Qwen 8.2%）同向支持：Llama 在 SciERC IE 上整体弱于 Qwen， 生成的 triples 更少且更保守，violation rate 低可能是 \\\"生成少 → 违反少\\\" 而非 \\\"更遵守约束\\\"。 Per-relation rank correlation 与 Qwen 约 0.82（Compare/Feature-of 仍是 top violators）， 说明 violation landscape 的 relative pattern 跨模型保持，但 absolute rates model-dependent。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED full S2 two-pass constrained decoding\",\n    \"description\": \"在 DocRED 上运行 S2：Pass 1 grammar-only entity extraction，Pass 2 基于 Pass 1 entities 编译 input-dependent grammar 后 relation extraction。验证 S2 在 96-relation ontology 上的表现。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents_checked\": 978,\n      \"total_triples\": 16800,\n      \"total_entities\": 19500,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.108,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.048,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0798,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.582,\n      \"latency_overhead_vs_unconstrained_pct\": 135,\n      \"dr_delta_vs_s1_pp\": 0.61\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"S1 vs S2 Cross-Dataset Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Dataset\",\n          \"S1_DR(%)\",\n          \"S2_DR(%)\",\n          \"S1_CF(%)\",\n          \"S2_CF(%)\",\n          \"S1_RF1(%)\",\n          \"S2_RF1(%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SciERC\",\n            0.93,\n            0.97,\n            9.9,\n            8.03,\n            8.36,\n            8.03\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DocRED (predicted)\",\n            10.19,\n            10.8,\n            2.99,\n            4.8,\n            8.17,\n            7.98\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED S2 的预期负面结果强化 \\\"S2 降为 appendix\\\" 的决策。 在 worst tier 下建议完全跳过——GPU 时间优先保障 DocRED unconstrained rerun 和 semantic_only（这两个是消融表 + enabling ratio 的必需数据）， S2 on DocRED 的 expected negative result 只增加论文中需要解释的 noise。 论文中处理为 \\\"S2 results on SciERC (Appendix A) show comparable performance to S1; we leave cross-dataset S2 evaluation to future work.\\\"\\n\\nS2 在 SciERC 上已确认无优势（DR 0.97% ≈ S1 0.93%，CF 8.03% ≈ S1 9.9%）。 DocRED 上预期同样无优势，原因： (a) S2 的 Pass 1 entity extraction 在 DocRED 上 error propagation 更严重——\\n    96 relations 意味着 Pass 2 的 input-dependent grammar 需要涵盖更多 relation type 的 constraints，\\n    Pass 1 的任何 entity type error 都会导致 Pass 2 constraint set 偏差；\\n(b) DocRED document 长度大（avg ~200 words），两次 full inference 的 token 总量翻倍，\\n    但 constraint quality 不提升；\\n(c) DR=10.8%（vs S1 10.19%）略差，因为 Pass 1 entity errors propagate：\\n    Pass 1 将 entity X 标注为 ORG，Pass 2 grammar 据此编译 ORG-compatible relations，\\n    但 X 实际是 LOC，导致 Pass 2 在 X 参与的 triples 上 enforce 了错误的 constraints；\\n(d) CF=4.8% 高于 S1 的 2.99%，因为 S2 的 entity registry 基于 Pass 1 output，\\n    而 Pass 2 的 relation extraction 可能 assign 不同 type（两个 pass 各自独立推理 type），\\n    within-pass consistency 比 single-pass 更难保证。\\n在 worst tier 下强烈建议不运行此实验——节省 ~16 GPU-hours 用于论文写作。 SciERC S2 data 已足够支持 \\\"S2 is architectural variant, not improvement\\\" 的 conclusion。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":604,"startLine":1,"totalLines":604}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Fo3YBxNBGytE3LmwWZTnwJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019z7fJSPG3AkbJxC7f9DfJG","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T094226/worst/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11802,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11802},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ebf8474-508b-47ef-8b53-5e664546d2e0","uuid":"cd291849-acff-409a-931e-9cc055c609a9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019z7fJSPG3AkbJxC7f9DfJG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\tEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Title\n7\tOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n8\t(Note: \"Guaranteed\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \"Near-Complete\" is honest and defensible.)\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\tLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero F1 cost** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n12\t\n13\t**Phase 2 confirmed**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%), and is **F1-neutral** (R-F1 +0.13pp, not statistically significant — correctly framed as \"zero cost\", not \"improvement\").\n14\t\n15\t## Core Claims\n16\t\n17\t### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\n18\tLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n19\t\n20\t**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n21\t\n22\t**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n23\t\n24\t### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\n25\tSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n26\t- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n27\t- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n28\t- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n29\t\n30\t**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n31\t\n32\t### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\n33\tOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n34\t1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n35\t2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n36\t\n37\tThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n38\t\n39\tThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n40\t\n41\t**Graceful degradation** (per Reviewer assessment, D008): When $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$ (semantic layer would mask all grammar-valid tokens), the system falls back to grammar-only control. Occurred 1/998 DocRED docs (0.1%), 0/551 SciERC sentences — consistent with tighter constraints increasing empty-intersection likelihood. Implementation is error recovery (fallback), NOT formal invariant guarantee. Do NOT frame as \"provable composition\" — fallback's existence is counter-evidence. Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; mention cross-dataset observation in §5 Discussion (1-2 sentences, N=1 too weak for dedicated analysis).\n42\t\n43\t**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n44\t- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n45\t- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n46\t- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n47\t\n48\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n49\t- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n50\t- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n51\t\n52\t**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n53\t\n54\t⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n55\t\n56\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n57\t\n58\t### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n59\t**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n60\t\n61\t### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n62\t**Response**: (a) Post-hoc wastes compute on invalid outputs (14-15% rejection rate); (b) cannot redirect probability mass to valid alternatives; (c) for streaming/real-time extraction, post-hoc filtering is too late. Post-hoc approaches (e.g., SHACL/DL reasoner-based validation, Alviano et al. IJCAI 2025 ASP-based structured knowledge verification) validate constraints after generation but cannot correct invalid outputs during decoding. ⚠️ 原引用 \"LLM+ASP (ICLP 2025)\" 已核实为不准确（venue/方法描述均有误），已修正。\n63\t\n64\t### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n65\t**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n66\t\n67\t### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n68\t**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n69\t\n70\t**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n71\t\n72\t### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n73\t**Response**: Phase 0 establishes methodology; cross-model validation (Llama-3.1-8B, 70B quantized) planned for Phase 2 if time permits. The constraint compiler is model-agnostic — only the tokenizer-specific first-token verification needs re-running per model.\n74\t\n75\t### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n76\t**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Phase 2 confirms F1-neutral**: S1 R-F1 0.0836 (+0.13pp vs unconstrained 0.0823), S2 R-F1 0.0803 (-0.20pp vs unconstrained). Both within noise on ~1700 triples. Frame as: \"Constraint enforcement is F1-neutral — extraction quality is preserved while violations are near-eliminated.\" Do NOT claim F1 improvement (single seed, no bootstrap CI). Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\n77\t\n78\t### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n79\t**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n80\t\n81\t**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n82\t- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n83\t- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n84\t- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n85\t\n86\t**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n87\t\n88\t**论证层次**：\n89\t1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n90\t2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n91\t3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n92\t4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n93\t\n94\t**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n95\t\n96\t**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n97\t\n98\t**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n99\t\n100\t### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n101\t**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n102\t\n103\t## Paper Structure (Draft)\n104\t1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n105\t2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n106\t3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n107\t4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n108\t5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n109\t6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n110\t7. Conclusion\n111\t\n112\t## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n113\t\n114\t**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n115\t- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n116\t- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\"\n117\t- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n118\t- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n119\t- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n120\t\n121\t**Claim with caution**:\n122\t- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n123\t- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n124\t- \"F1 improvement\" — NOT statistically significant, frame as F1-neutral only\n125\t- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n126\t\n127\t**Do NOT claim**:\n128\t- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n129\t- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n130\t- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n131\t- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n132\t- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n133\t- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n134\t- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n135\t\n136\t## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n137\t\n138\t1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n139\t2. **Single model limitation** (MEDIUM-HIGH): Only Qwen3-8B tested. Mitigation: Llama-3.1-8B cross-model validation if time permits.\n140\t3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n141\t4. **DocRED Phase 2 weak** (MEDIUM): If constrained decoding on DocRED (96 types) shows weaker gains or higher CF, claim generality is weakened.\n142\t5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral. No longer a risk.\n143\t\n144\t## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n145\t\n146\t- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 complete ✅ + Phase 1 integration ✅\n147\t- **May 14 (now)**: Phase 2 SciERC core results confirmed ✅ (unconstrained/grammar/semantic/full_s1). full_s2 running, DocRED Phase 2 starting.\n148\t- **May 15-17**: DocRED Phase 2 (grammar_only + full_s1) + S2 analysis + CF deep dive + Evaluate-for error cases\n149\t- **May 17-19**: Cross-model (Llama-3.1-8B) if time permits + ablation gaps\n150\t- **May 19-24**: Paper writing (Paper Agent) + submission\n151\t\n152\t**Current bottleneck**: DocRED Phase 2 cross-dataset validation. GPU 0 should be running DocRED grammar_only NOW.\n153\t\n154\t## Status\n155\t- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n156\t- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n157\t- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n158\t- Phase 2 SciERC S1: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓94%, F1-neutral)\n159\t- Phase 2 SciERC S2: ✅ Complete (551/551, DR=0.97%, CF=8.03%, R-F1=8.03% — no advantage over S1)\n160\t- Phase 2 DocRED: 🔄 grammar_only running on cuda:0 (29/998)\n161\t- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9%, S2 8.03%, both from independent per-relation enforcement)\n162\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ebf8474-508b-47ef-8b53-5e664546d2e0","uuid":"b6b4707c-ac7a-4bf2-88e5-bc2e4c76789e","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:37:21.704Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T094226/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n\n## Title\nOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n(Note: \"Guaranteed\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \"Near-Complete\" is honest and defensible.)\n\n## Core Insight\nLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero F1 cost** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n\n**Phase 2 confirmed**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%), and is **F1-neutral** (R-F1 +0.13pp, not statistically significant — correctly framed as \"zero cost\", not \"improvement\").\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\nLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n\n**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n\n**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\nSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n\n**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n\n### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\nOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n\nThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n\nThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n\n**Graceful degradation** (per Reviewer assessment, D008): When $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$ (semantic layer would mask all grammar-valid tokens), the system falls back to grammar-only control. Occurred 1/998 DocRED docs (0.1%), 0/551 SciERC sentences — consistent with tighter constraints increasing empty-intersection likelihood. Implementation is error recovery (fallback), NOT formal invariant guarantee. Do NOT frame as \"provable composition\" — fallback's existence is counter-evidence. Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; mention cross-dataset observation in §5 Discussion (1-2 sentences, N=1 too weak for dedicated analysis).\n\n**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n\n**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n\n⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n\n### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n**Response**: (a) Post-hoc wastes compute on invalid outputs (14-15% rejection rate); (b) cannot redirect probability mass to valid alternatives; (c) for streaming/real-time extraction, post-hoc filtering is too late. Post-hoc approaches (e.g., SHACL/DL reasoner-based validation, Alviano et al. IJCAI 2025 ASP-based structured knowledge verification) validate constraints after generation but cannot correct invalid outputs during decoding. ⚠️ 原引用 \"LLM+ASP (ICLP 2025)\" 已核实为不准确（venue/方法描述均有误），已修正。\n\n### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n\n### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n\n**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n\n### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n**Response**: Phase 0 establishes methodology; cross-model validation (Llama-3.1-8B, 70B quantized) planned for Phase 2 if time permits. The constraint compiler is model-agnostic — only the tokenizer-specific first-token verification needs re-running per model.\n\n### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **Phase 2 confirms F1-neutral**: S1 R-F1 0.0836 (+0.13pp vs unconstrained 0.0823), S2 R-F1 0.0803 (-0.20pp vs unconstrained). Both within noise on ~1700 triples. Frame as: \"Constraint enforcement is F1-neutral — extraction quality is preserved while violations are near-eliminated.\" Do NOT claim F1 improvement (single seed, no bootstrap CI). Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\n\n### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n\n**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n\n**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n\n**论证层次**：\n1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n\n**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n\n**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n\n**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n\n### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (Draft)\n1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n7. Conclusion\n\n## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n\n**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\"\n- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n\n**Claim with caution**:\n- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n- \"F1 improvement\" — NOT statistically significant, frame as F1-neutral only\n- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n\n**Do NOT claim**:\n- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n\n## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n\n1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n2. **Single model limitation** (MEDIUM-HIGH): Only Qwen3-8B tested. Mitigation: Llama-3.1-8B cross-model validation if time permits.\n3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n4. **DocRED Phase 2 weak** (MEDIUM): If constrained decoding on DocRED (96 types) shows weaker gains or higher CF, claim generality is weakened.\n5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral. No longer a risk.\n\n## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n\n- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 complete ✅ + Phase 1 integration ✅\n- **May 14 (now)**: Phase 2 SciERC core results confirmed ✅ (unconstrained/grammar/semantic/full_s1). full_s2 running, DocRED Phase 2 starting.\n- **May 15-17**: DocRED Phase 2 (grammar_only + full_s1) + S2 analysis + CF deep dive + Evaluate-for error cases\n- **May 17-19**: Cross-model (Llama-3.1-8B) if time permits + ablation gaps\n- **May 19-24**: Paper writing (Paper Agent) + submission\n\n**Current bottleneck**: DocRED Phase 2 cross-dataset validation. GPU 0 should be running DocRED grammar_only NOW.\n\n## Status\n- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n- Phase 2 SciERC S1: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓94%, F1-neutral)\n- Phase 2 SciERC S2: ✅ Complete (551/551, DR=0.97%, CF=8.03%, R-F1=8.03% — no advantage over S1)\n- Phase 2 DocRED: 🔄 grammar_only running on cuda:0 (29/998)\n- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9%, S2 8.03%, both from independent per-relation enforcement)\n","numLines":162,"startLine":1,"totalLines":162}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Q9ozMJr3jCwGUJvygxo79Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full picture. Let me understand the narrative pivot for the \"worst\" tier:\n\n1. **Title**: \"How LLMs Violate Ontology Constraints: A Landscape Study and Grammar-Based Mitigation\"\n2. **Three independent contributions**:\n   - (1) Violation Landscape Study (40% of paper) — first systematic measurement across ontology complexity\n   - (2) Grammar-constrained decoding as universal zero-cost structural validity layer (ET→0%, RV→0%)\n   - (3) Semantic layer as tight ontology proof-of-concept (with explicit \"scaling to complex ontologies remains open\")\n\n\n3. DocRED shows 10.19% residual error rate as an open problem, and the null result on tightness becomes an empirical finding worth reporting. I'll move the S1/S2 comparison to the appendix and frame this as an empirical study with a targeted solution rather than a methods paper, aiming for EMNLP 2026's empirical analysis track.\n\nNow I'm sketching the paper structure: the abstract will position this as an empirical study plus grammar mitigation, the introduction establishes that LLMs systematically violate ontology constraints and we're studying this landscape while proposing grammar-based fixes, and the background covers IE ontology structure and grammar-constrained decoding before diving into the violation landscape study as the main ~40% contribution.\n\nFor the violation landscape section, I'm setting up experiments with SciERC (7 relations) and DocRED (96 relations) using Qwen3-8B, establishing a violation taxonomy across entity type, relation value, domain, and constraint failures. Then I'll show unconstrained violation rates, analyze per-relation distributions with constraint tightness, compare against Llama-3.1-8B, and examine the tightness-DR correlation that works on SciERC but fails on DocRED.\n\nThe grammar-constrained decoding section compiles the ontology into XGrammar to eliminate entity type and relation value violations entirely while adding only ~14% latency overhead. Then I'm prototyping a semantic constraint layer with a type processor to handle the remaining violations.\n\nNow I'm looking at the semantic constraint results—domain/range constraints reduce domain violations dramatically on SciERC (from 15.4% down to 0.93%, a 94% reduction) but show much weaker gains on DocRED (15.8% down to 10.19%, only 35.5% reduction). The enabling dependency effect is strong on SciERC but nearly absent on DocRED, and I need to address the constraint failure side effects. After that, I'll discuss the DocRED residual violations as an open problem, revisit the tightness-DR null result, and note constraint failures as an inherent limitation before moving into related work and conclusions.\n\nNow I'm pulling the experiment data to write the LaTeX carefully, particularly the DocRED Phase 2 ablation table with the violation metrics and performance numbers.\n\nGenerating markdown table... Generating markdown table... Now I'm looking at the rank correlation between models at 0.82, then examining the breakdown of different error types in the DocRED dataset—entity-value relations are the most common issue at nearly 2%, followed by entity duplication and hallucinated triples. The latency analysis shows that adding grammar constraints increases processing time by about 14% while reducing throughput slightly.\n\nGenerating performance comparison tables... Now I'm pulling together the SciERC ablation results from different sources in the data—the unconstrained numbers show higher error rates across the board compared to the constrained S1 setup, and I can see the semantic-only component contributes significantly to the overall performance gap. Let me reconstruct the full ablation picture by combining what's available across the cross-model comparisons and the framing analysis. I'm realizing I don't have the complete Grammar-only ablation numbers for SciERC, so I'll work with the available data points—the semantic-only and full model results—and focus the detailed ablation breakdown on DocRED where I have the full table. Now I need to plan out the paper structure.\n\nI'm organizing this around a clear narrative: start with the violation taxonomy and experimental setup, then dedicate the bulk of the paper to the landscape study showing how violations vary across models and ontologies, follow that with the grammar-constrained decoding approach that eliminates structural violations entirely, and finish with the semantic constraint layer for handling tighter ontologies. I'm settling on the paper structure and deciding to write it in LaTeX using a standard article format since this is for review purposes rather than formal submission.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16830,"cache_read_input_tokens":23249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16830},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ebf8474-508b-47ef-8b53-5e664546d2e0","uuid":"9870e661-3900-4d60-a274-bda63af70d25"}
